-- ownership: a function value handed to JavaScript escapes what it captured
-- (`ownership-checker.md` §18.6; §15 decision 6). `Debug.toString` hands its
-- argument to `Js.pure` inside a lambda, so its summary escapes it — `J`,
-- the conservative rule until Change 5's words exist — and a list shown and
-- then extended is rejected `escaped`, the line saying it is this rule.
pub shown : List Int → Int
shown xs =
    s = Debug.toString xs
    ys = [ …xs, 1 ]
    String.length s + List.length ys
